const e="kentucky-state-fair-talent-classic",c=2026,t="Built from the 2026 brochure (2 pages). It prints no entry fee, no street address, no contact person or phone number, no judging criteria and no prize split by place; the venue name and the fair dates are printed on the cover only. Past winners' names (2025) are personal data and are not copied. The brochure says anyone aged 22 and up may enter; the template band for that division is 22-99. The Grand Award rule applies to ages 13-21 only. The Request for Sanction form and Entry Form are mentioned but not linked in the brochure.",a={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"Kentucky State Fair Talent Classic 2026: solo and group acts in three age divisions, on {{EventDates}}.",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"Rules were revised for 2026. Only winners of a sanctioned 2026 preliminary can compete at the State Fair. Any act that runs more than 4 minutes loses 1 point for every second over.",Notes:["Read all the rules carefully; they were revised for 2026.","Latest information: {{MoreInfoLink}}."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General",Items:["The Talent Classic shows talented youth from across Kentucky in three age divisions: 7-12, 13-21 and 22 and up.","The contest began in 1979. Its only purpose is to find, develop and encourage young amateur entertainers.","Entries are accepted in these solo or group categories: Vocal, Instrumental, Variety, Dance and Acrobatic/Gymnastic.","The decision of the judges is final.","All contestants, parents, teachers and friends must follow the general rules and regulations of the Kentucky State Fair, found at {{MoreInfoLink}}.","All questions about entries, category, rules or any other issue are decided by the Talent Classic staff of the Kentucky State Fair. Their decision is final.","The Kentucky State Fair does not organize the preliminary events.","Baton twirlers and similar acts that use batons or machetes are not accepted.","No fire, smoke or smoke effect is allowed on the State Fair stage. Acts must stay on the stage.","Contestants use only the lighting system provided by the Fair.","Contestants use only the sound system and the sound operator provided by the Kentucky State Fair. You may use your own amplifiers.","Pirated music does not work in the sound system. All background music must be on a CD or a USB drive.","Any act that runs more than 4 minutes receives a 1-point scoring penalty for every second over.","An official timekeeper is present at all State Fair competitions. Timing starts with the first word, note or movement and ends with the last word, note or movement. This includes bows and encores."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Who can enter",Items:["All State Fair contestants must be winners of Kentucky State Fair in-person or virtual preliminaries that are sanctioned for 2026.","All contestants must be at least 7 years old on {{AgeCutoffDate}}. This includes everyone who has visual importance in the act, except piano accompanists.","The three age divisions are 7-12, 13-21 and 22 and up.","The contest is not open to professionals.","A professional is anyone who is a union member, has a professional manager or booking agent, or earns the principal and supporting income from performing.","A contestant may enter only once in any one category at the State Fair and may enter a total of two categories.","If a performer won an invitation to the State Fair from a preliminary, he or she must not perform the same act, or enter the same category, in another preliminary.","If a performer wins a finals invitation in two categories at the preliminaries, he or she must choose one of the two categories for the final performance.","An act may drop a member who is listed on the entry form. It must not add or replace any member listed on the form.","A person cannot be part of an act at the State Fair if that person did not perform in the act at the preliminary.","No member of a Grand Award winning act may compete again in the same category. This applies to ages 13-21 only."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to enter",Items:["Enter through a Kentucky State Fair sanctioned preliminary contest. The brochure prints no direct entry route to the State Fair.","Each sanctioned preliminary names three overall winners. Fourth and fifth place winners are named as alternates. There are no ties.","The preliminary producer or chairperson marks the placement on the entry forms of the top five winners and mails them to the Kentucky State Fair within three working days of the preliminary date.","Contestants must not mail their entry forms to the Fair. The producer or chairperson gets the entry forms of the top five winning acts to the State Fair office.","All preliminary paperwork and videos must reach the Kentucky State Fair within three days of the preliminary, for the act to be eligible for the 2026 State Fair.","Each chairperson sends a video (DVD, USB drive or MP4) of each contestant's performance to the State Fair before {{VideoDeadline}}.","The Kentucky State Fair staff will view acts and suggest a category by appointment before {{CategoryAdviceDeadline}}.","Special exception requests for instrumental accompaniment must be filed in writing before {{CategoryAdviceDeadline}}."]},{Key:"levels",Title:"Preliminaries and the State Fair",Items:["Preliminary contests are held throughout the state, in person or virtually, and each one must be sanctioned every year by the Kentucky State Fair.","Only talent competitions are sanctioned. Recitals and the talent divisions of beauty contests are not sanctioned.","A group that wants to produce a preliminary must fill in the Request for Sanction Form Information Sheet and all other forms completely and return them to the Kentucky State Fair at least 2 weeks before its contest. Sanction is not granted before this.","No sanction is given to single-person productions.","No producer or chairperson may advertise a contest as a sanctioned Kentucky State Fair event until a written Official Sanction Letter is received from the Fair.","All acts must be judged in the preliminary competition. Special entertainment at the preliminary cannot be considered for State Fair competition.","The top 3 winners of sanctioned preliminaries are guaranteed an invitation to the Kentucky State Fair Talent Classic, if they are eligible.","If any of the top 3 winners is unable or not eligible to enter, the Fair takes the fourth place winner, if eligible, as an official Fair entry.","Each county fair or organization in the Talent Classic produces only one preliminary contest per age category.","If several sessions are needed for the number of participants, the organization is advised to hold one final preliminary event to choose the contestants who go to the State Fair. Any exception must be approved in advance by Kentucky State Fair staff.","At the preliminary, all contestants must be judged and at least two judges must be present.","All preliminary judges must be 21 years old or older. They must not include a State Fair representative, and a State Fair representative must not be present during deliberation.","A State Fair representative who is present may be asked about rule clarification only.","There must be no discussion of the contest between judges and contestants, teachers or parents before or during the preliminary.","No son, daughter, grandchild, step-child or other relative of a preliminary contest worker may enter the contest in which the relative works.","Chairpersons must read all rules and give the brochure to all contestants, and point out General Rules 6, 9, 10 and 13 and the Variety definition."]},{Key:"fees",Title:"Fees",Items:["{{SanctionFee}}","The brochure prints no entry fee for contestants."]},{Key:"dates",Title:"Dates",Items:["The Talent Classic is held on {{EventDates}}.","The 2026 Kentucky State Fair runs from {{FairDates}}.","Contestants must be at least 7 years old on {{AgeCutoffDate}}."]},{Key:"venue",Title:"Venue",Items:["The Kentucky State Fair is held at {{Venue}}."]},{Key:"prizes",Title:"Prizes",Items:["The 2026 Kentucky State Fair awards {{PrizeTotal}}.","Winners are invited to a State Fair showcase performance.","In 2025 the ages 13-21 division had a Grand Award winner and 1st to 4th place Sweepstakes placings, and the 7-12 and 22+ divisions each had a 1st place winner. The brochure prints no prize split by place for 2026."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Conduct",Items:["No teachers, parents, friends or audience members may be on the stage at the Kentucky State Fair.","Only one person other than those visible on the stage may be backstage for each act. This includes all parents, teachers and friends.","A contestant is disqualified and loses all ribbons and prize money won up to that time for any discourtesy to a judge or official of the Fair.","A contestant is also disqualified and loses ribbons and prize money if the contestant, a parent, a teacher or a friend tries to communicate with the judges before, during or after their adjudications."]},{Key:"judging",Title:"Judging",Items:["The decision of the judges is final.","The brochure prints no judging criteria or marks."]},{Key:"reporting",Title:"After the preliminary",Items:["The producer or chairperson of each preliminary sends the entry forms of the top five winners to the State Fair as set out in the sanction agreement."]},{Key:"other",Title:"Penalties and liability for preliminaries",Items:["If a chairperson or preliminary worker breaks any printed rule, the Kentucky State Fair revokes the sanction and may disqualify acts.","If entry forms or other required paperwork are not sent by the set date, future sanction is denied.","The Kentucky State Fair Board, its agents, servants and employees take no responsibility for damages in the production of any preliminary.","Any Hold Harmless form used by a preliminary must have the prior written permission of the Kentucky State Fair."]}],Documents:[{Title:"2026 Talent Classic brochure (PDF)",Url:"https://kystatefair.org/static_assets/2625bc5b-c3d0-47f4-b6ad-b197fb000943/KSFTC-Brochure-Print.pdf"},{Title:"Talent Classic web page",Url:"https://kystatefair.org/talent-classic"}]},n=[{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"General Rules 12",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["A group may drop a member listed on the entry form, but must not add or replace any member.","A person cannot be part of the act at the State Fair if that person did not perform in the act at the preliminary."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- A group may drop a member listed on the entry form, but must not add or replace any member.
- A person cannot be part of the act at the State Fair if that person did not perform in the act at the preliminary.`}],o=[{AgeGroup:"Ages 13-21 Solo",Source:"General Rules 18",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["No member of a Grand Award winning act may compete again in the same category."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- No member of a Grand Award winning act may compete again in the same category.`},{AgeGroup:"Ages 13-21 Group",Source:"General Rules 18",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["No member of a Grand Award winning act may compete again in the same category."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- No member of a Grand Award winning act may compete again in the same category.`}],r=[{Title:"Vocal",Source:"Category Description: Vocal; General Rules 6",Sections:{About:["A performance by a vocalist or vocalists."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["An instrumental accompaniment by the performer or others is allowed, but it must be only an accompaniment. The test is whether the performance would stand alone if the accompaniment were removed."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:["No voice, voices, record or tape with any vocal background may be used for accompaniment. This includes recorded live voices and synthetically produced and recorded voices, such as synthesizers or digital sampling.","Lip-syncing is not allowed.","Accompaniment tracks with any background vocals are strictly prohibited."],Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- A performance by a vocalist or vocalists.

## Rules
- An instrumental accompaniment by the performer or others is allowed, but it must be only an accompaniment. The test is whether the performance would stand alone if the accompaniment were removed.

## Not allowed
- No voice, voices, record or tape with any vocal background may be used for accompaniment. This includes recorded live voices and synthetically produced and recorded voices, such as synthesizers or digital sampling.
- Lip-syncing is not allowed.
- Accompaniment tracks with any background vocals are strictly prohibited.`},{Title:"Instrumental",Source:"Category Description: Instrumental Solo or Group; General Rules 8",Sections:{About:["A solo or group instrumental performance without vocal utterance."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["In an instrumental solo, the only accompaniment allowed is a live or taped acoustical piano. Special exception requests must be filed in writing before {{CategoryAdviceDeadline}}.","If the instrument is piano, no accompaniment is allowed.","When an electronic keyboard is used, the contestant must create all sound live on stage."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- A solo or group instrumental performance without vocal utterance.

## Rules
- In an instrumental solo, the only accompaniment allowed is a live or taped acoustical piano. Special exception requests must be filed in writing before {{CategoryAdviceDeadline}}.
- If the instrument is piano, no accompaniment is allowed.
- When an electronic keyboard is used, the contestant must create all sound live on stage.`},{Title:"Dance",Source:"Category Description: Dance Solo and Ensemble; General Rules 7",Sections:{About:["A performance by a dancer or dancers."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Accompanists are allowed on stage, but they must not have visual importance in the performance.","Acrobatics or gymnastics are judged in another category.","Vocal performances are not judged."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:["A dancer must not use a taped recording with taps or a clear tap effect."],Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- A performance by a dancer or dancers.

## Rules
- Accompanists are allowed on stage, but they must not have visual importance in the performance.
- Acrobatics or gymnastics are judged in another category.
- Vocal performances are not judged.

## Not allowed
- A dancer must not use a taped recording with taps or a clear tap effect.`},{Title:"Acrobatic/Gymnastic",Source:"Category Description: Acrobatic/Gymnastic Solo or Group",Sections:{About:["A solo or group performance."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["At least one-third of the performance must be acrobatics or gymnastics, and no more than two-thirds may be acrobatic or gymnastic movements.","The performance must be choreographed."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- A solo or group performance.

## Rules
- At least one-third of the performance must be acrobatics or gymnastics, and no more than two-thirds may be acrobatic or gymnastic movements.
- The performance must be choreographed.`},{Title:"Variety",Source:"Category Description: Variety; General Rules 23",Sections:{About:["A performance by one or more persons. This category is a showcase for acts that are not listed in any other category, for example a ventriloquist, a juggler or a comedian."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["All persons who have visual importance in the act must meet the age qualification of the Talent Classic.","Assignment to this category is at the discretion of the State Fair.","Performers who fit the description of another category may not appear in the Variety category.","A vocalist or vocal group that accompanies themselves would not normally meet the Variety test."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["Chairpersons must tell contestants about the Variety definition."]},Markdown:`## About this competition
- A performance by one or more persons. This category is a showcase for acts that are not listed in any other category, for example a ventriloquist, a juggler or a comedian.

## Rules
- All persons who have visual importance in the act must meet the age qualification of the Talent Classic.
- Assignment to this category is at the discretion of the State Fair.
- Performers who fit the description of another category may not appear in the Variety category.
- A vocalist or vocal group that accompanies themselves would not normally meet the Variety test.

## Notes for participants
- Chairpersons must tell contestants about the Variety definition.`}],i=[],s=[{Key:"EventDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Talent Classic dates",Value:"Saturday 22 and Sunday 23 August 2026",Source:"2026 Brochure, cover"},{Key:"FairDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Kentucky State Fair dates",Value:"August 20-30, 2026",Source:"2026 Brochure, cover"},{Key:"AgeCutoffDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Age check date (minimum age 7)",Value:"2026-08-01",Source:"General Rules 2"},{Key:"VideoDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Preliminary performance videos due before",Value:"2026-07-31",Source:"2026 Brochure, Preliminary Contest Requirements 18"},{Key:"CategoryAdviceDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Category suggestions by appointment and special accompaniment requests before",Value:"2026-08-01",Source:"General Rules 8 and 23"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Event venue",Value:{Name:"Kentucky Expo Center",Address:"",City:"",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"2026 Brochure, cover"},{Key:"PrizeTotal",Kind:"prize",Label:"Cash prizes",Value:"more than $5,000 in cash prizes",Source:"2026 Brochure, introduction"},{Key:"SanctionFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Sanction fee",Value:"There is no fee for sanction of a preliminary contest.",Source:"2026 Brochure, introduction"},{Key:"MoreInfoLink",Kind:"link",Label:"Organiser web page",Value:"kystatefair.org/talent-classic",Source:"General Rules 21; closing line"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"News printed in the brochure",Value:[{Date:"",Title:"Now open to all ages",Text:"The Talent Classic is now open to all ages, with three divisions: 7-12, 13-21 and 22 and up.",Url:""},{Date:"",Title:"Rules revised for 2026",Text:"The General Rules were revised for 2026. Read them carefully.",Url:""}],Source:"2026 Brochure, cover and General Rules"}],l=[{Claim:"Rules, eligibility, preliminary requirements, penalties, liability, dates and prize total are taken from the organiser's 2026 brochure.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Kentucky State Fair Talent Classic 2026 brochure",Url:"https://kystatefair.org/static_assets/2625bc5b-c3d0-47f4-b6ad-b197fb000943/KSFTC-Brochure-Print.pdf"}],u={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:t,Page:a,ParticipantTypes:n,AgeGroups:o,Competitions:r,CompetitionAgeGroups:i,Variables:s,Evidence:l};export{o as AgeGroups,i as CompetitionAgeGroups,r as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,a as Page,n as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,s as Variables,c as Year,u as default};
